Well, teleport and teleport control cease being useful once you hit the
first plane, so don't sweat those too much once you hit the upstairs on
level 1.

I'd consider spending a few hundred turns using wands/scrolls of create
monster to camp a shrine for a bit and try to earn some more protection, as
well as any useful death drops. However, it sounds like you've picked up
the Amulet already, and a couple hundred turns of enduring remote curses
and summoned nasties would be somewhat aggravating.


Personally, I think 1 low charged wand of death isn't enough. If you have
to visit all 3 altars on the Astral, you're probably going to need to zap
the riders a couple times each (barring Death himself of course0, plus any
other nuisance creatures (like Rodney).

A blessed archon figurine wouldn't be a terrible idea. Yes, the portals are
one way, but with a magic whistle it's pretty simple to make sure they stay
with you. Just need to be careful on Water, since the portal moves around.

Overall, I'd say you'll get the most rewards from a magic marker, write up
a charging scroll first to recharge the marker, then churn out some enchant
armor scrolls until everything you're wearing is at +4 or +5. Get a
replacement shirt if you can.

On the astral, consider reverse genociding purple worms, taming them, and
teleporting them around so they can ingest some substantial number of your
opponents. if they can eat a dozen or so of the priests, this will go far
in making your life easier.


